  "docs": {
    "allowance/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# allowance.get\n\nRead one allowance by its id: organization, member, limit, spent, state.\n\n**Who may call:** the grantee of the allowance, or the owner of its organization.\n\n**A read:** answered from the records, with no handler.\n\n**Budget:** p95 50ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | allowance.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | allowance.organization |\n| member | allowance.member |\n| limit | allowance.limit |\n| spent | allowance.spent |\n| state | text |\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the grantee of the allowance, or the owner of its organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme allowance get --id <id>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /allowance/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.allowance.get(payload)`.\n",
    "allowance/grant.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# allowance.grant\n\nLet a member spend from the organisation, up to a limit each month.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its organization.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 200ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | allowance.organization |\n| member | allowance.member |\n| limit | allowance.limit |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| allowance | allowance.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`grant`: from nothing (it creates) to active, emitting AllowanceGranted.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `allowance.grant.insert` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AllowanceLimitTooHigh | 44 | AL-003 | declared in errors.ts, carrying cap |\n| PersonNotFound | 4 | PE-901 | nothing has the id in member; the handler never runs; carries `id` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme allowance grant --organization <organization> --member <member> --limit <limit>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /allowance/grant` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.allowance.grant(payload)`.\n",
    "allowance/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# allowance\n\nMoney a member may spend from their organisation, up to a limit each month.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| member | person.id |\n| limit | Amount |\n| spent | Amount |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: active, exhausted, revoked. A move from the wrong state is refused AllowanceNotActive (exit 40).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| grant | (creates) | active | AllowanceGranted |\n| spend | active | active, exhausted | AllowanceSpent |\n| revoke | active, exhausted | revoked | AllowanceRevoked |\n\n## Roles\n\n- grantee\n\n## Operations\n\n- [allowance.get](get.md): Read one allowance by its id: organization, member, limit, spent, state.\n- [allowance.grant](grant.md): Let a member spend from the organisation, up to a limit each month.\n- [allowance.revoke](revoke.md): Stop an allowance. Nothing more can be spent from it.\n- [allowance.spend](spend.md): Spend from what is left of this month's allowance.\n",
    "allowance/revoke.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# allowance.revoke\n\nStop an allowance. Nothing more can be spent from it.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its allowance.organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| allowance | allowance.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`revoke`: from active or exhausted to revoked, emitting AllowanceRevoked.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `allowance.revoke.update` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AllowanceNotActive | 40 | AL-900 | the allowance is in a state revoke can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its allowance.organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme allowance revoke --allowance <allowance>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /allowance/revoke` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.allowance.revoke(payload)`.\n",
    "allowance/spend.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# allowance.spend\n\nSpend from what is left of this month's allowance.\n\n**Who may call:** the grantee of the allowance.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| allowance | allowance.id |\n| amount | Amount |\n| memo | Memo |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| remaining | Amount |\n\n## Move\n\n`spend`: from active to active or exhausted, emitting AllowanceSpent.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `allowance.spend.load` (database)\n- `allowance.spend.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AllowanceExceeded | 41 | AL-001 | declared in errors.ts, carrying remaining |\n| AllowanceNotActive | 40 | AL-900 | the allowance is in a state spend can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the grantee of the allowance; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme allowance spend --allowance <allowance> --amount <amount> --memo <memo>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /allowance/spend` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.allowance.spend(payload)`.\n",
    "api-key/create.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# api-key.create\n\nCreate an API key in an organisation. The key itself is shown once.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 250ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | api-key.organization |\n| name | api-key.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| apiKey | api-key.id |\n| key | Secret (secret) |\n\n## Steps\n\n- `api-key.create.issue` (database)\n- `api-key.create.insert` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme api-key create --organization <organization> --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /api-key/create` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.api-key.create(payload)`.\n",
    "api-key/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# api-key\n\nA key an agent or a service calls with, on behalf of whoever created it. Better Auth keeps its hash.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| name | text |\n| createdBy | person.id |\n\n## Operations\n\n- [api-key.create](create.md): Create an API key in an organisation. The key itself is shown once.\n",
    "invitation/accept.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation.accept\n\nAccept an invitation and become a member of its organisation.\n\n**Who may call:** the invitee of the invitation.\n\n**Budget:** p95 200ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| invitation | invitation.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | invitation.organization |\n| membership | membership.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`accept`: from pending to accepted, emitting InvitationAccepted.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `invitation.accept.join` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| InvitationNotPending | 40 | IN-900 | the invitation is in a state accept can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the invitee of the invitation; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme invitation accept --invitation <invitation>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /invitation/accept` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.invitation.accept(payload)`.\n",
    "invitation/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation\n\nAn offer to join an organisation, sent to an email address.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| email | person.email |\n| invitedBy | person.id |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: pending, accepted, revoked. A move from the wrong state is refused InvitationNotPending (exit 40).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| send | (creates) | pending | InvitationSent |\n| accept | pending | accepted | InvitationAccepted |\n| revoke | pending | revoked | InvitationRevoked |\n\n## Roles\n\n- invitee\n\n## Operations\n\n- [invitation.accept](accept.md): Accept an invitation and become a member of its organisation.\n- [invitation.revoke](revoke.md): Withdraw an invitation that hasn't been accepted.\n- [invitation.send](send.md): Invite someone to an organisation by email.\n",
    "invitation/revoke.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation.revoke\n\nWithdraw an invitation that hasn't been accepted.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its invitation.organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| invitation | invitation.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`revoke`: from pending to revoked, emitting InvitationRevoked.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `invitation.revoke.update` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| InvitationNotPending | 40 | IN-900 | the invitation is in a state revoke can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its invitation.organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme invitation revoke --invitation <invitation>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /invitation/revoke` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.invitation.revoke(payload)`.\n",
    "invitation/send.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# invitation.send\n\nInvite someone to an organisation by email.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of its organization.\n\n**Budget:** p95 200ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | invitation.organization |\n| email | invitation.email |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| invitation | invitation.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`send`: from nothing (it creates) to pending, emitting InvitationSent.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `invitation.send.insert` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of its organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme invitation send --organization <organization> --email <email>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /invitation/send` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.invitation.send(payload)`.\n",
    "membership/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# membership.get\n\nRead one membership by its id: organization, person, role.\n\n**Who may call:** the holder of the membership, or the owner of its membership.organization.\n\n**A read:** answered from the records, with no handler.\n\n**Budget:** p95 50ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | membership.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | membership.organization |\n| person | membership.person |\n| role | membership.role |\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the holder of the membership, or the owner of its membership.organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme membership get --id <id>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /membership/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.membership.get(payload)`.\n",
    "membership/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# membership\n\nA person's place in an organisation.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| organization | organization.id |\n| person | person.id |\n| role | Role |\n\n## Roles\n\n- holder\n\n## Operations\n\n- [membership.get](get.md): Read one membership by its id: organization, person, role.\n",
    "organization/create.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# organization.create\n\nFound an organisation with its cap. Whoever founds it owns it, and is its first member.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone signed in.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 250ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | organization.name |\n| cap | organization.cap |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| organization | organization.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`create`: from nothing (it creates) to active, emitting OrganizationCreated.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `organization.create.insert` (database)\n- `organization.create.owner` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't anyone signed in; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme organization create --name <name> --cap <cap>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /organization/create` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.organization.create(payload)`.\n",
    "organization/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# organization.get\n\nRead one organization by its id: name, owner, state.\n\n**Who may call:** the owner of the organization.\n\n**A read:** answered from the records, with no handler.\n\n**Budget:** p95 50ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | organization.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | organization.name |\n| owner | organization.owner |\n| state | text |\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the owner of the organization; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nacme organization get --id <id>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /organization/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.organization.get(payload)`.\n",
